1
00:00:05,871 --> 00:00:07,323
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,348 --> 00:00:08,914
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:17,886 --> 00:00:20,061
(Episode 22)

4
00:00:25,070 --> 00:00:28,623
It seemed ridiculous at first,
but I think you're right.

5
00:00:29,411 --> 00:00:33,085
Nobody gets out of life alive anyway,
so I'll try everything I never got to do,

6
00:00:33,359 --> 00:00:39,098
stop worrying about what people think,
and live freely. Like you.

7
00:00:42,455 --> 00:00:46,590
Mic check.

8
00:00:51,150 --> 00:00:56,415
Here's something I've never told anyone.
I actually wanted to be a rock star.

9
00:00:58,076 --> 00:01:00,436
<i>It was dark</i>

10
00:01:02,004 --> 00:01:08,956
<i>My past was hard</i>

11
00:01:09,265 --> 00:01:13,838
<i>But if my past</i>

12
00:01:13,863 --> 00:01:17,552
<i>Is something I can love</i>

13
00:01:17,646 --> 00:01:22,026
<i>If a picture of my memories</i>

14
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:28,053
<i>Is something I can draw</i>

15
00:01:28,186 --> 00:01:31,708
<i>March forward</i>

16
00:01:31,733 --> 00:01:35,333
<i>March forward</i>

17
00:01:35,387 --> 00:01:41,479
- <i>We keep on marching</i>
- Give it up!

18
00:01:42,048 --> 00:01:45,642
<i>I'm going to sing</i>

19
00:01:45,710 --> 00:01:48,884
- <i>Missing it every day</i>
- What are you doing?

20
00:01:48,909 --> 00:01:54,117
<i>Until the morning comes</i>

21
00:01:54,142 --> 00:01:58,175
<i>Let's all march</i>

22
00:01:59,337 --> 00:02:00,865
March!

23
00:02:00,890 --> 00:02:02,649
Under the Minor Offenses Act, Article 3,
Paragraph 1, Subparagraph 21,

24
00:02:02,674 --> 00:02:04,956
you were reported for a noise disturbance.

25
00:02:05,787 --> 00:02:09,415
- What? A minor offense?
- Yes.

26
00:02:09,637 --> 00:02:11,990
What offense? I was just singing.

27
00:02:12,224 --> 00:02:13,704
I was only busking.

28
00:02:13,729 --> 00:02:20,428
The person who reported you said
it wasn't singing, just painful noise.

29
00:02:20,453 --> 00:02:22,194
And we got multiple reports.

30
00:02:22,277 --> 00:02:24,711
Noise?

31
00:02:25,504 --> 00:02:28,718
Didn't you officers come here
to hear me sing?

32
00:02:29,363 --> 00:02:32,942
<i>I'm going to sing</i>

33
00:02:32,967 --> 00:02:35,123
<i>With you every day</i>

34
00:02:35,322 --> 00:02:36,815
I'm sorry.

35
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:38,761
<i>Until the morning</i>

36
00:02:44,104 --> 00:02:46,864
So I can't sing if I'm bad at it?

37
00:02:46,964 --> 00:02:49,087
Lots of fans stayed till the end, too.

38
00:02:50,291 --> 00:02:52,545
Do you need good chopstick skills to eat?

39
00:02:53,430 --> 00:02:54,873
<i>Chopsticks</i>

40
00:02:54,947 --> 00:02:57,780
<i>Good with chopsticks</i>

41
00:02:57,890 --> 00:03:01,519
Honestly, my voice wasn't
in great shape today.

42
00:03:02,047 --> 00:03:03,311
It just wasn't my day.

43
00:03:07,473 --> 00:03:12,924
Should I just swim across
the Korea Strait and back?

44
00:03:13,377 --> 00:03:16,070
Keep that up, and you'll get arrested.

45
00:03:22,078 --> 00:03:23,869
It's gotten so cold.

46
00:03:29,572 --> 00:03:34,849
But when I think about how nobody
gets out of life alive anyway,

47
00:03:34,982 --> 00:03:36,769
there's so much I want to do now.

48
00:03:37,017 --> 00:03:38,253
Should I get piercings?

49
00:03:38,830 --> 00:03:43,405
Pierce my nose, my lips,
and my eyebrow right here.

50
00:03:43,631 --> 00:03:47,293
I saw people with piercings the other day,
and they looked so brave and cool.

51
00:03:48,478 --> 00:03:49,592
Should I get a tattoo?

52
00:03:49,617 --> 00:03:51,933
One that runs from my ear down to my neck.

53
00:03:55,131 --> 00:03:58,743
- Are you messing with me?
- What?

54
00:03:59,210 --> 00:04:01,047
You're messing with me on purpose.

55
00:04:02,011 --> 00:04:03,964
"If you can run, I can fly."

56
00:04:04,691 --> 00:04:06,693
"I'm one step ahead of you, Han Gyu Rim."

57
00:04:07,798 --> 00:04:09,457
Is this payback?

58
00:04:10,033 --> 00:04:11,464
Payback? No.

59
00:04:12,983 --> 00:04:16,010
Aren't you embarrassed?
Aren't you ashamed of me?

60
00:04:16,751 --> 00:04:21,290
After I humiliated you like that
and pulled every childish, crazy stunt,

61
00:04:21,375 --> 00:04:23,835
shouldn't you be fed up
and running for the hills by now?

62
00:04:30,043 --> 00:04:31,609
You think I've never run away?

63
00:04:32,136 --> 00:04:34,368
After you dumped me eight years ago,
I was so bitter...

64
00:04:34,988 --> 00:04:38,834
I went to the States and Italy
to forget you,

65
00:04:39,508 --> 00:04:42,174
went to the ends of the earth,
and did all kinds of crazy things.

66
00:04:43,463 --> 00:04:44,844
I don't do that kind of stuff anymore.

67
00:04:46,017 --> 00:04:48,583
No matter what you do on purpose,

68
00:04:49,271 --> 00:04:52,711
I won't misunderstand,
and I won't run away.

69
00:04:55,924 --> 00:05:02,001
I just can't outsmart you, Mu Jin.

70
00:05:03,591 --> 00:05:05,376
There's no way I can win.

71
00:05:07,740 --> 00:05:08,977
Gyu Rim.

72
00:05:13,824 --> 00:05:18,549
I'm feeling really down right now,
so I'll call you later.

73
00:05:18,590 --> 00:05:20,076
Gyu Rim.

74
00:05:38,710 --> 00:05:40,587
Thank you.

75
00:05:46,564 --> 00:05:50,583
Here, Ok Seon!
Sausage and rice cake skewers!

76
00:05:51,703 --> 00:05:52,703
Here.

77
00:05:53,170 --> 00:05:55,957
So this is what they look like?

78
00:05:55,982 --> 00:05:57,711
You've never seen these before either?

79
00:06:03,924 --> 00:06:07,682
It's good. It's really good.

80
00:06:10,993 --> 00:06:13,250
This Han River ramen is good too.

81
00:06:13,398 --> 00:06:17,674
I had no idea the Han River
had changed this much.

82
00:06:17,825 --> 00:06:22,724
You must've been too busy running
your sashimi restaurant to come out here.

83
00:06:23,370 --> 00:06:26,150
I'll take you out a lot from now on.

84
00:06:26,221 --> 00:06:31,614
If I hadn't met you, I'd have missed out
on half the world.

85
00:06:32,524 --> 00:06:34,910
Are you sure running a sashimi place
isn't a lie?

86
00:06:35,984 --> 00:06:37,549
It's not a lie.

87
00:06:38,078 --> 00:06:41,542
Are you sure you don't live
in a fish tank at a sashimi place?

88
00:06:41,903 --> 00:06:44,265
Swimming around with the flounder
and sea bream.

89
00:06:45,024 --> 00:06:49,042
You're not a frog in a well.
You're Ok Seon in a fish tank.

90
00:06:51,047 --> 00:06:52,476
What are you talking about?

91
00:06:52,501 --> 00:06:53,977
Excuse me.

92
00:06:54,683 --> 00:06:59,643
I really need to use the restroom.
Could you watch my grandkid for a moment?

93
00:06:59,668 --> 00:07:02,460
- Sure, go ahead.
- Thank you.

94
00:07:02,737 --> 00:07:05,726
Careful, don't wet yourself.
Take your time.

95
00:07:07,524 --> 00:07:09,669
Let's see.

96
00:07:10,277 --> 00:07:14,019
Look at this tough little guy.

97
00:07:15,244 --> 00:07:18,182
Or is it a little princess?

98
00:07:18,207 --> 00:07:19,479
Why are you crying so much?

99
00:07:19,604 --> 00:07:21,599
Why are you making the baby cry?

100
00:07:23,858 --> 00:07:26,751
Don't cry, sweetie.

101
00:07:26,864 --> 00:07:29,429
I'll push your stroller for you.

102
00:07:30,009 --> 00:07:34,993
If you keep crying,
Santa won't bring you any presents.

103
00:07:41,650 --> 00:07:43,784
You're good with kids.

104
00:07:44,616 --> 00:07:46,962
You must babysit your grandkids a lot.

105
00:07:49,597 --> 00:07:54,238
What would you do if it turned out
Mu Jin had a son?

106
00:07:55,491 --> 00:07:59,955
I think I saw Mu Jin's son today, Mom.

107
00:08:03,030 --> 00:08:06,555
No. I've never seen one.

108
00:08:09,333 --> 00:08:10,820
So you don't have grandkids.

109
00:08:11,235 --> 00:08:16,041
Well, you don't look old enough
to be called Grandma yet.

110
00:08:17,111 --> 00:08:22,591
I don't look old enough to be called
Grandpa either, but I have a grandson.

111
00:08:25,337 --> 00:08:28,327
It looks like I do have a grandson,

112
00:08:30,031 --> 00:08:32,357
but I've never seen his face. Not once.

113
00:08:32,677 --> 00:08:34,270
What's that supposed to mean?

114
00:08:37,610 --> 00:08:42,960
So the son who walked out on you
over some woman had a son.

115
00:08:45,863 --> 00:08:49,591
Hey, then isn't it game over?

116
00:08:49,631 --> 00:08:54,135
If she had his son, you have to accept her
as your daughter-in-law, like it or not.

117
00:08:56,237 --> 00:09:00,351
Forget it. If that fails,
I'll just take my grandson.

118
00:09:10,011 --> 00:09:15,426
Mu Jin called while you were showering.
On your cell phone.

119
00:09:15,859 --> 00:09:16,917
Okay.

120
00:09:35,490 --> 00:09:39,568
I bought you that, right?
For your birthday.

121
00:09:39,593 --> 00:09:44,433
That's right. How could you afford
such nice cosmetics?

122
00:09:44,578 --> 00:09:49,332
I saved up my New Year's money
and allowance to buy them for you.

123
00:09:50,210 --> 00:09:52,516
Da Som's mom uses it too.

124
00:09:53,777 --> 00:09:57,088
Really? So it's Da Som's mom's pick.

125
00:09:57,324 --> 00:09:59,296
That must be why it's super moisturizing.

126
00:10:00,596 --> 00:10:03,005
Doesn't my skin look like it's glowing?

127
00:10:03,184 --> 00:10:05,145
It's glowing, Mom.

128
00:10:08,430 --> 00:10:11,223
When I talked to Mu Jin on the phone,

129
00:10:11,336 --> 00:10:17,338
I asked him not to hate you too much,
even if you act weird with him.

130
00:10:18,664 --> 00:10:22,188
Gyeol, do you like Mu Jin that much?

131
00:10:41,220 --> 00:10:44,274
- Hello, Gyu Rim.
- Did you get home okay?

132
00:10:45,361 --> 00:10:48,094
No, not yet. Yeah.

133
00:10:49,627 --> 00:10:52,827
I talked to Gyeol earlier,
and he said you were in the shower.

134
00:11:03,961 --> 00:11:05,761
I have a favor to ask, Mu Jin.

135
00:11:06,627 --> 00:11:08,227
Sure. Ask away.

136
00:11:10,061 --> 00:11:11,761
Anything but telling me to get lost.

137
00:11:15,940 --> 00:11:19,740
Make up with your mother.

138
00:11:23,061 --> 00:11:28,927
If loving me means cutting ties
with your mother, I don't want that.

139
00:11:31,861 --> 00:11:38,127
My dad got into so much trouble,
but he never abandoned us.

140
00:11:38,794 --> 00:11:40,327
That's why we still live together.

141
00:11:43,494 --> 00:11:46,160
No matter how much I love you,

142
00:11:47,006 --> 00:11:49,413
I can't be with you
if you've abandoned your family.

143
00:11:50,394 --> 00:11:53,594
No, I won't.

144
00:11:56,494 --> 00:11:59,194
No matter how much you love me,

145
00:12:01,661 --> 00:12:07,961
I don't think I'm worth
cutting ties with your mother over.

146
00:12:10,594 --> 00:12:11,627
Gyu Rim.

147
00:12:11,661 --> 00:12:16,104
Make up with your mother
and get her blessing.

148
00:12:17,427 --> 00:12:23,027
Until you get it,
a hundred years, a thousand years,

149
00:12:24,724 --> 00:12:26,094
I'll wait.

150
00:12:43,164 --> 00:12:50,080
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

151
00:12:53,173 --> 00:12:54,661
Honey.

152
00:12:54,861 --> 00:12:58,263
I heard the food here is great,
so I came early. Too early, I guess.

153
00:12:58,288 --> 00:12:59,916
Let's go in.

154
00:13:19,194 --> 00:13:20,565
Thank you.

155
00:13:21,527 --> 00:13:23,153
Haven't you eaten?

156
00:13:23,586 --> 00:13:26,246
Slow down. You'll get indigestion.

157
00:13:27,587 --> 00:13:29,493
It's because the food here is so good.

158
00:13:29,647 --> 00:13:31,874
I think we should have
our company dinners here from now on.

159
00:13:37,066 --> 00:13:39,298
I have something to tell you.

160
00:13:42,834 --> 00:13:47,434
Can you have tea with me
during the break later?

161
00:13:49,408 --> 00:13:50,741
Sure.

162
00:13:53,278 --> 00:13:54,427
A divorce?

163
00:14:02,427 --> 00:14:06,627
It's strange to hear that from you.

164
00:14:09,494 --> 00:14:10,527
Why?

165
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:16,350
It's not because of you,

166
00:14:18,017 --> 00:14:20,624
and definitely not because of Seo Hyeon.

167
00:14:23,094 --> 00:14:26,994
It's because of me. All this time,

168
00:14:29,827 --> 00:14:33,994
I was wearing clothes
that didn't suit me at all.

169
00:14:36,027 --> 00:14:41,127
To everyone else, they probably looked
gorgeous, dazzling, and glamorous,

170
00:14:44,261 --> 00:14:50,827
but honestly, the whole time I wore them,
I felt anxious and uncomfortable.

171
00:14:53,527 --> 00:14:57,694
Now that I've taken them off,
I feel so comfortable and free.

172
00:15:04,427 --> 00:15:06,461
I don't need any alimony.

173
00:15:06,861 --> 00:15:08,441
All these years, thanks to you,

174
00:15:10,926 --> 00:15:12,860
I've had it so good
I can barely hold my head up.

175
00:15:15,861 --> 00:15:18,394
More than enough.

176
00:15:20,974 --> 00:15:24,207
Even if I lived ten more lives,

177
00:15:26,427 --> 00:15:28,561
I couldn't repay
the kindness you've shown me,

178
00:15:31,794 --> 00:15:33,727
not even half of it.

179
00:15:46,727 --> 00:15:48,151
Honey, let's do this.

180
00:15:49,700 --> 00:15:52,367
There's something I need to take care of
right now...

181
00:15:54,361 --> 00:15:57,390
Right. It's something only I can handle,

182
00:15:58,004 --> 00:15:59,564
so once that's over...

183
00:16:00,494 --> 00:16:04,427
Once I'm done with that,
let's talk again then.

184
00:16:06,861 --> 00:16:08,961
- Hun Tae.
- Let's do that.

185
00:16:09,447 --> 00:16:14,281
Yes, all right. About the divorce,

186
00:16:16,760 --> 00:16:19,027
let's keep it from Seo Hyeon for now,

187
00:16:20,027 --> 00:16:23,994
and when I've wrapped everything up,
I'll let you know.

188
00:16:24,561 --> 00:16:26,061
Let's talk again then.

189
00:16:27,361 --> 00:16:30,883
Just wait a little until then.
Can you do that?

190
00:16:41,661 --> 00:16:44,363
Hey, Han Gyu Yeong. Gyu Yeong.

191
00:16:52,261 --> 00:16:54,883
- What time is it?
- It's 3:10 p.m.

192
00:16:55,127 --> 00:16:58,394
I slept for seven hours.

193
00:16:59,161 --> 00:17:01,561
Isn't today Sunday?
Why are you at the office?

194
00:17:01,794 --> 00:17:03,527
For a cosmetics ad shoot.

195
00:17:04,194 --> 00:17:07,248
Anyway, did you sleep
at the office last night?

196
00:17:07,435 --> 00:17:09,335
You're wearing the same outfit
as yesterday.

197
00:17:15,727 --> 00:17:17,762
It all came out.

198
00:17:17,796 --> 00:17:21,103
That I swapped my dad
and lied that my family was rich.

199
00:17:21,574 --> 00:17:24,259
So? Hey, did you get kicked out?

200
00:17:31,934 --> 00:17:35,011
- Yes, this is Han Gyu Yeong.
- This is Jang Hun Tae.

201
00:17:40,207 --> 00:17:44,026
- Surprised I called out of the blue?
- Not at all.

202
00:17:51,561 --> 00:17:56,890
Your in-laws seem to have figured it out.
Did you know?

203
00:18:01,061 --> 00:18:02,761
How did you find out, sir?

204
00:18:04,861 --> 00:18:07,461
Your father-in-law came to my office.

205
00:18:12,394 --> 00:18:16,227
They knew from the start.
That I swapped my dad...

206
00:18:18,227 --> 00:18:23,727
They knew I lied that you were my father,
but played along on purpose.

207
00:18:26,401 --> 00:18:27,847
I see.

208
00:18:29,348 --> 00:18:32,181
They were playing the long game.

209
00:18:33,227 --> 00:18:34,294
What do you mean?

210
00:18:39,227 --> 00:18:41,761
Try not to be too shocked
by what I'm about to tell you.

211
00:18:45,132 --> 00:18:50,527
I had someone look into it,
and as for your in-laws,

212
00:18:51,894 --> 00:18:55,461
one has four fraud convictions,
the other three.

213
00:18:55,993 --> 00:19:00,093
They've also served time for extortion,
threats, and defamation.

214
00:19:00,827 --> 00:19:03,527
And your husband, Kang Seong Uk...

215
00:19:04,627 --> 00:19:08,761
has a record of assaulting
ex-girlfriends and women he lived with.

216
00:19:09,127 --> 00:19:11,194
Three of those cases led to charges.

217
00:19:12,127 --> 00:19:14,492
Couldn't you be mistaken?

218
00:19:14,838 --> 00:19:16,818
Maybe you looked into the wrong people?

219
00:19:19,661 --> 00:19:21,527
Get a grip and listen to me.

220
00:19:23,894 --> 00:19:28,593
Your father-in-law's business is
a paper company, just an empty shell.

221
00:19:29,561 --> 00:19:31,148
Your mother-in-law said
she runs a gallery, right?

222
00:19:31,181 --> 00:19:32,648
That's no gallery.

223
00:19:33,427 --> 00:19:36,635
She ran an unlicensed bar in Gangnam.

224
00:19:37,507 --> 00:19:44,425
And the house they live in isn't theirs.
They started paying rent there recently.

225
00:19:45,427 --> 00:19:47,272
Even worse,

226
00:19:49,594 --> 00:19:54,361
the woman your husband lived with
before he met you,

227
00:19:55,794 --> 00:19:58,094
he's still keeping a second home with her.

228
00:20:06,161 --> 00:20:10,361
This is so humiliating.

229
00:20:12,261 --> 00:20:14,294
So what I'm trying to say is,

230
00:20:15,161 --> 00:20:19,227
can't you end this marriage now,
before it's too late?

231
00:20:19,687 --> 00:20:21,621
If there's anything I can do, I'll help.

232
00:20:24,994 --> 00:20:27,146
How would you help me?

233
00:20:29,161 --> 00:20:33,894
Like a father stepping in for his kid.
Like any normal dad would.

234
00:20:33,961 --> 00:20:38,594
If you want me to grab him and hit him,
I will. I'd even pull his hair out.

235
00:20:38,927 --> 00:20:40,427
You're not even my father.

236
00:20:40,461 --> 00:20:42,194
Who says? Who says I'm not your father?

237
00:20:44,161 --> 00:20:47,461
I married your mother.
As her husband, I'm your father too.

238
00:20:50,461 --> 00:20:55,127
Gyu Yeong, we didn't con anyone.

239
00:20:56,527 --> 00:20:57,959
I am your father.

240
00:20:58,300 --> 00:21:01,387
And from now on, I plan to be your father
with my head held high.

241
00:21:02,868 --> 00:21:07,898
So until you, my daughter,
find your footing...

242
00:21:09,294 --> 00:21:12,294
and become happier,

243
00:21:13,861 --> 00:21:18,094
I'll stand by you as your father,
right alongside your birth father.

244
00:21:19,194 --> 00:21:22,261
It's the least I can do.

245
00:21:33,261 --> 00:21:35,061
Did your boyfriend give you this?

246
00:21:35,241 --> 00:21:37,508
No, my mother-in-law did.

247
00:21:44,627 --> 00:21:45,827
Aren't you going to check it?

248
00:21:46,461 --> 00:21:49,673
- No need. It's fake.
- What?

249
00:21:50,321 --> 00:21:54,036
Don't just glance at it.
Take a closer look.

250
00:21:54,061 --> 00:21:58,355
I'd bet my right hand that it's fake.
No, I'd bet this whole store on it.

251
00:22:16,794 --> 00:22:18,494
Are you okay? Did you get hurt?

252
00:22:18,594 --> 00:22:20,894
What do I do? My hand slipped.

253
00:22:21,394 --> 00:22:23,161
Don't move. Stay right there.

254
00:22:27,827 --> 00:22:29,527
- Gyu Min, step out for a second.
- Okay.

255
00:22:33,494 --> 00:22:35,261
That cup was Han Gyu Yeong's.

256
00:22:35,961 --> 00:22:39,261
Some limited-edition designer cup.
She wouldn't even let us touch it.

257
00:22:40,094 --> 00:22:43,627
Whether it's designer or not,
she can't take it with her when she dies.

258
00:22:43,685 --> 00:22:45,027
That dummy.

259
00:22:47,227 --> 00:22:48,775
Something feels off.

260
00:22:49,002 --> 00:22:51,576
Nothing happened to Han Gyu Yeong, did it?

261
00:22:52,192 --> 00:22:55,666
If something happened, she'd have called.

262
00:22:58,161 --> 00:23:01,094
You always worry about Han Gyu Yeong too.

263
00:23:01,861 --> 00:23:04,394
She's always right here in your head.

264
00:23:04,827 --> 00:23:07,689
"Is she doing okay in her marriage?"

265
00:23:09,461 --> 00:23:11,579
Gyeol's probably here,

266
00:23:12,853 --> 00:23:15,440
Han Gyu Seo and I are here,

267
00:23:16,427 --> 00:23:19,827
and Han Gyu O's here, right?

268
00:23:26,294 --> 00:23:28,161
What are you doing, Dad?

269
00:23:29,061 --> 00:23:31,061
You actually went and got that?

270
00:23:31,668 --> 00:23:33,960
Since you've been acting strange lately,

271
00:23:34,093 --> 00:23:37,400
dad thinks you've been possessed
by Han Gyu Yeong's spirit.

272
00:23:38,861 --> 00:23:42,094
I'm fine now. I'm back to normal, Dad.

273
00:23:43,460 --> 00:23:47,168
You're right.
I guess you're not possessed.

274
00:23:47,940 --> 00:23:51,052
I'm sorry I acted out of character
and threw you off.

275
00:23:51,152 --> 00:23:52,736
It won't happen again.

276
00:23:52,761 --> 00:23:56,161
See? She says she's fine.

277
00:23:56,894 --> 00:23:59,237
You guys said she was acting weird too.

278
00:23:59,627 --> 00:24:02,566
You were so worried about Gyu Rim
you even held a meeting.

279
00:24:04,827 --> 00:24:08,682
But Dad, why did you go
to the Han River last night?

280
00:24:09,461 --> 00:24:11,427
Why did you have Han River ramen?

281
00:24:14,094 --> 00:24:17,861
And you had a mini kimchi pack
with the ramen.

282
00:24:18,861 --> 00:24:23,327
And sausage and rice cake skewers too,
with lots of sauce?

283
00:24:24,894 --> 00:24:27,411
What are you? Who are you?

284
00:24:28,464 --> 00:24:29,824
Did it go in here?

285
00:24:30,727 --> 00:24:33,161
Get out of my Gyu Min, you evil spirit!

286
00:24:34,727 --> 00:24:35,861
What's wrong with this thing?

287
00:24:36,840 --> 00:24:38,673
Did you see him at the Han River?

288
00:24:39,194 --> 00:24:40,727
No, I was at my part-time job yesterday.

289
00:24:40,827 --> 00:24:42,894
Then how do you know?

290
00:24:43,661 --> 00:24:48,594
How would you know I had Han River ramen
and skewers unless you're a ghost?

291
00:24:49,527 --> 00:24:50,794
How did you know?

292
00:24:51,261 --> 00:24:54,861
I saw a receipt in his pants pocket
when I put them in the washer.

293
00:24:55,607 --> 00:24:58,518
A receipt for Han River ramen and skewers.

294
00:25:01,519 --> 00:25:02,882
You scared me.

295
00:25:03,496 --> 00:25:05,595
Of all people, you're pulling a prank
on me?

296
00:25:05,876 --> 00:25:07,402
You know how easily I get scared.

297
00:25:10,861 --> 00:25:12,594
I need to take some calming pills.

298
00:25:17,127 --> 00:25:19,794
Thank you for the citron rice cakes.
They were delicious.

299
00:25:20,114 --> 00:25:25,907
I'd love to return the favor, so come by
the restaurant with your girlfriend.

300
00:25:28,087 --> 00:25:29,961
Please knock before you come in.

301
00:25:30,394 --> 00:25:33,694
Hey, why would I need to knock
to come into my son's room?

302
00:25:34,113 --> 00:25:36,899
- Where's Gyu O?
- He left for his part-time job at dawn.

303
00:25:37,094 --> 00:25:39,123
He went to work at dawn?

304
00:25:39,536 --> 00:25:40,882
What's gotten into him all of a sudden?

305
00:25:40,907 --> 00:25:42,974
It's good that he's working so hard.

306
00:25:44,827 --> 00:25:49,861
Would it kill you to talk nicely
to me? Is it against the law?

307
00:25:50,427 --> 00:25:52,361
You little punk, honestly.

308
00:25:56,264 --> 00:25:57,561
Nice.

309
00:26:00,661 --> 00:26:01,794
Why are you taking Gyu O's clothes?

310
00:26:02,127 --> 00:26:06,527
I don't have anything decent to wear,
so I'm borrowing a few. Why?

311
00:26:06,961 --> 00:26:08,361
Why would you borrow his clothes?

312
00:26:08,727 --> 00:26:11,694
I just told you.
I don't have anything decent to wear.

313
00:26:11,727 --> 00:26:14,827
Even so, why wear his clothes?
Who are you trying to impress?

314
00:26:14,894 --> 00:26:18,127
I'm trying to impress the whole country.
Why? Happy now?

315
00:26:20,061 --> 00:26:21,094
Are you seeing a woman?

316
00:26:21,394 --> 00:26:25,527
I see women, I see men...

317
00:26:25,661 --> 00:26:27,294
Aren't you scared of women?

318
00:26:27,394 --> 00:26:29,127
You're the one who scares me most.

319
00:26:29,161 --> 00:26:31,061
After what you went through,
aren't you sick of it?

320
00:26:32,894 --> 00:26:38,261
You think all women are like that,
but it's just your mom. Only her.

321
00:26:38,961 --> 00:26:41,327
How do you know there's not another one?

322
00:26:41,427 --> 00:26:43,227
Sure, there might be.

323
00:26:43,627 --> 00:26:46,818
There might be,
but this woman is different.

324
00:26:46,972 --> 00:26:49,432
Ok Seon is the real deal.

325
00:26:52,627 --> 00:26:53,927
This one.

326
00:26:56,994 --> 00:27:02,061
Fine, call me petty, call me small-minded,

327
00:27:02,261 --> 00:27:05,294
but please stop inviting me
to your grandkids' first birthdays.

328
00:27:05,994 --> 00:27:12,294
I went to all of your kids' weddings.
Isn't that enough?

329
00:27:12,427 --> 00:27:14,594
Can you really not take a hint?

330
00:27:15,133 --> 00:27:18,996
And honestly, are we that close?

331
00:27:19,271 --> 00:27:21,337
We're not that close.

332
00:27:22,061 --> 00:27:24,861
Hey, if you're hurt, too bad.
If you think I'm cold, too bad.

333
00:27:25,227 --> 00:27:28,861
I'm not going to the party,
so pass that on to everyone else.

334
00:27:29,261 --> 00:27:34,961
Anyone who sends me an invitation
to a first birthday party is out.

335
00:27:37,694 --> 00:27:39,861
You could've just sent a gold ring.

336
00:27:40,261 --> 00:27:42,610
Why make a call like that, Mom?

337
00:27:42,724 --> 00:27:44,744
Do you know what gold costs these days?

338
00:27:45,261 --> 00:27:49,994
Who even throws first birthday parties
these days? It's so tacky.

339
00:27:50,061 --> 00:27:52,861
They should just take some pictures,
sing a song, and call it a day.

340
00:27:52,927 --> 00:27:55,827
Why bother other people?

341
00:28:05,061 --> 00:28:09,661
My kids aren't even married, and if
they had a baby, I'd never see it...

342
00:28:10,794 --> 00:28:17,061
Forget a gold ring. With a mom like that,
he probably didn't even get a party.

343
00:28:31,461 --> 00:28:33,027
(Personal Profile, Han Gyeol,
mother Han Gyu Rim)

344
00:28:48,194 --> 00:28:49,416
Yes, Secretary Ahn.

345
00:28:49,441 --> 00:28:55,780
The kid Han Gyu Rim is raising
was named Han Gyeol, right?

346
00:28:56,994 --> 00:29:00,327
Could I meet that kid?

347
00:29:02,527 --> 00:29:05,238
Make up with your mother
and get her blessing.

348
00:29:06,061 --> 00:29:11,127
Until you get it, I'll wait
a hundred years, a thousand years.

349
00:29:17,994 --> 00:29:22,094
(Mother)

350
00:29:33,394 --> 00:29:34,794
What a sigh.

351
00:29:38,761 --> 00:29:39,794
Long time.

352
00:29:43,127 --> 00:29:44,161
It's been a while.

353
00:29:45,794 --> 00:29:47,461
I'm fine.

354
00:29:48,827 --> 00:29:53,494
I was nervous about running into you,
but I'm surprisingly okay.

355
00:29:54,261 --> 00:29:57,136
Honestly, I'm kind of impressed
with how chill I'm being.

356
00:29:57,194 --> 00:29:59,894
Just come by anytime.
Jeong Woo's here too.

357
00:29:59,961 --> 00:30:01,644
Actually, I came to see Jeong Woo.

358
00:30:01,724 --> 00:30:03,751
He's my go-to person for venting.

359
00:30:05,661 --> 00:30:07,094
Should I tell him to come down?

360
00:30:08,761 --> 00:30:11,061
Are things going well with Han Gyu Rim?

361
00:30:15,861 --> 00:30:17,261
Well, you know.

362
00:30:18,694 --> 00:30:20,461
It must be really hard for you two.

363
00:30:21,761 --> 00:30:25,761
The road ahead won't be easy.
I honestly feel sorry for you.

364
00:30:26,694 --> 00:30:30,261
Cheering you on is a stretch,
but I won't curse you anymore.

365
00:30:32,694 --> 00:30:33,827
Want me to make you a coffee?

366
00:30:33,894 --> 00:30:37,727
Yes, lots of ice and two extra shots.
Strong and cold.

367
00:30:39,733 --> 00:30:42,039
- You want coffee too?
- Yes, hand drip.

368
00:30:51,861 --> 00:30:55,827
Isn't it hard seeing Mu Jin?
Are you really okay?

369
00:30:59,600 --> 00:31:01,187
I was so mad yesterday I thought I'd die.

370
00:31:01,268 --> 00:31:03,482
Sit down first.
I have so much to tell you.

371
00:31:04,127 --> 00:31:06,261
Did I tell you I even got scolded
by a high schooler?

372
00:31:08,116 --> 00:31:09,361
You did.

373
00:31:11,361 --> 00:31:16,002
You kept me up last night talking
for two hours and 40 minutes.

374
00:31:16,027 --> 00:31:19,327
When I woke up this morning,
I almost drew a police sketch of that kid.

375
00:31:19,361 --> 00:31:21,061
The more I think about it,
the angrier I get.

376
00:31:21,227 --> 00:31:23,561
Who is he to chew me out like that?

377
00:31:23,761 --> 00:31:25,027
I went on a blind date, Seo Hyeon.

378
00:31:25,694 --> 00:31:28,827
A blind date? You never mentioned it.

379
00:31:29,127 --> 00:31:31,294
You were too busy talking.

380
00:31:31,594 --> 00:31:34,061
My father's health suddenly got worse,

381
00:31:34,127 --> 00:31:37,294
so he wants me to get married
this year, no matter what.

382
00:31:39,761 --> 00:31:40,860
No way.

383
00:31:40,885 --> 00:31:44,375
You're getting married out of nowhere,
without any warning?

384
00:31:44,407 --> 00:31:45,507
Don't kid around.

385
00:31:46,741 --> 00:31:52,374
Luckily, she seems to like me too.
And I don't mind her either.

386
00:31:53,861 --> 00:31:59,227
But she said she's fine with everything
except me having female friends,

387
00:31:59,327 --> 00:32:00,927
saying there's no such thing as friendship
between a man and a woman.

388
00:32:01,594 --> 00:32:03,894
She asked me to sort things out.

389
00:32:04,794 --> 00:32:08,161
What? Did she time-travel
from the Joseon era?

390
00:32:12,373 --> 00:32:17,727
I don't want the woman I'm marrying
to get the wrong idea.

391
00:32:19,087 --> 00:32:25,454
So from now on, unless it's serious,
don't call, text, or message me.

392
00:32:35,817 --> 00:32:36,817
Let's go in.

393
00:32:38,463 --> 00:32:40,004
Hello. How are you?

394
00:32:40,297 --> 00:32:42,004
- You're here?
- How have you been?

395
00:32:42,032 --> 00:32:43,032
Good.

396
00:32:43,091 --> 00:32:46,319
- Here it is.
- Why here? To buy clothes?

397
00:32:46,562 --> 00:32:49,504
No. I'm taking over this store.

398
00:32:49,617 --> 00:32:51,837
My parents left it to me
and told me to give it a shot.

399
00:32:52,403 --> 00:32:55,279
They say it has a bright future
if I work hard.

400
00:32:55,687 --> 00:32:58,847
Good for you. It suits you.

401
00:32:59,586 --> 00:33:01,060
Congratulations.

402
00:33:02,884 --> 00:33:04,178
Let's do it together, Gyu O.

403
00:33:05,285 --> 00:33:06,664
Do what together? Me?

404
00:33:08,117 --> 00:33:10,526
I can't. I don't have what it takes.

405
00:33:10,863 --> 00:33:13,212
I told my parents everything about you.

406
00:33:13,836 --> 00:33:15,965
From you saving me from Son Ji Yeol,

407
00:33:16,614 --> 00:33:19,046
to how you've lived because of me.

408
00:33:19,776 --> 00:33:23,771
So my parents said to give you
half of this store.

409
00:33:24,851 --> 00:33:26,986
They really hope you won't turn it down.

410
00:33:28,397 --> 00:33:33,031
They want us to make a fresh start
together at this store.

411
00:33:33,695 --> 00:33:36,152
Still, how can I accept this?

412
00:33:37,417 --> 00:33:38,951
I really can't. No.

413
00:33:39,704 --> 00:33:41,111
Should I have my parents come?

414
00:33:41,869 --> 00:33:44,784
Should I have them come
and persuade you in person?

415
00:33:51,604 --> 00:33:53,731
- Hold on.
- Okay.

416
00:33:55,657 --> 00:33:58,969
- Yes, Su Nam.
- My love, Gyu O.

417
00:33:59,676 --> 00:34:02,822
Are you busy this evening?

418
00:34:03,564 --> 00:34:07,440
Unless it's your parents' funeral,
cancel everything and make some time.

419
00:34:07,817 --> 00:34:09,442
What's going on all of a sudden?

420
00:34:09,467 --> 00:34:11,847
And don't you dare say no.

421
00:34:11,872 --> 00:34:14,484
You need to tell me what it is first...

422
00:34:14,485 --> 00:34:17,125
You have to say yes first.

423
00:34:17,864 --> 00:34:20,571
I'm an old woman, and this is my first
and last request. So?

424
00:34:20,957 --> 00:34:22,665
Yes or no?

425
00:34:24,777 --> 00:34:26,021
Okay, I'll be there.

426
00:34:26,827 --> 00:34:28,577
You said yes.

427
00:34:28,966 --> 00:34:33,084
If you go back on your word,
you'll be sorry.

428
00:34:40,520 --> 00:34:42,596
What is it?

429
00:34:43,267 --> 00:34:44,824
What are you doing with Gyu O?

430
00:34:45,377 --> 00:34:46,977
That's none of your business.

431
00:34:47,512 --> 00:34:51,156
Mr. Song. I'm going home for a bit,

432
00:34:51,181 --> 00:34:52,874
so watch the shop for me.

433
00:34:53,143 --> 00:34:55,080
Yes, ma'am. See you later.

434
00:34:58,512 --> 00:35:01,849
What's that old lady up to?

435
00:35:15,016 --> 00:35:16,317
Nice.

436
00:35:20,672 --> 00:35:24,448
Isn't the artist Joel amazing?

437
00:35:25,722 --> 00:35:28,289
He is. He's totally my type.

438
00:35:32,297 --> 00:35:34,663
How's Han Gyu Yeong doing?

439
00:35:35,244 --> 00:35:37,758
She's a newlywed, so it must be
all honey these days, right?

440
00:35:39,057 --> 00:35:44,194
Not honey. More like she got stung
by 1,000 bees all at once.

441
00:36:01,464 --> 00:36:02,464
What's this?

442
00:36:02,892 --> 00:36:05,094
Running away because you're scared
I'll sue you for fraud?

443
00:36:05,443 --> 00:36:07,267
The divorce papers are on the vanity.

444
00:36:07,303 --> 00:36:09,367
I've already signed everything,
so you just need to sign.

445
00:36:10,237 --> 00:36:11,687
Who said you could get divorced?

446
00:36:14,303 --> 00:36:17,048
Want me to list, one by one,

447
00:36:17,073 --> 00:36:18,730
every con you and your parents
pulled on me?

448
00:36:19,117 --> 00:36:20,886
Your parents are ex-cons with records
for fraud and extortion,

449
00:36:20,888 --> 00:36:23,170
and they're flat broke. And you?

450
00:36:25,172 --> 00:36:27,277
I don't even want to say it.
It'd dirty my mouth.

451
00:36:30,056 --> 00:36:31,364
Fine.

452
00:36:31,747 --> 00:36:33,783
We both conned each other,

453
00:36:34,052 --> 00:36:37,776
so we're two of a kind.
Let's just live happily ever after, then.

454
00:36:41,590 --> 00:36:43,607
There's one thing I'm curious about.

455
00:36:44,437 --> 00:36:46,583
If you knew I was lying,

456
00:36:46,631 --> 00:36:48,898
you must've known my family
had nothing either.

457
00:36:49,525 --> 00:36:50,980
Why did you marry me?

458
00:36:51,224 --> 00:36:52,537
What did you think you'd get out of me?

459
00:36:52,597 --> 00:36:54,004
What do you mean? There's plenty.

460
00:36:54,243 --> 00:36:56,685
There's Chairman Jang Hun Tae.
Your mom's husband.

461
00:36:57,457 --> 00:37:00,119
What's Chairman Jang got to do with me?

462
00:37:00,144 --> 00:37:01,444
We're not even close.

463
00:37:01,476 --> 00:37:03,750
I first met him when I asked him
to stand in when our parents met.

464
00:37:05,543 --> 00:37:08,116
I don't care. You choose.

465
00:37:08,477 --> 00:37:10,250
Either live with me ten more years,

466
00:37:10,491 --> 00:37:12,561
or if you want to split up,

467
00:37:12,836 --> 00:37:14,597
pay me three million dollars.

468
00:37:14,622 --> 00:37:15,844
You're crazy.

469
00:37:16,201 --> 00:37:18,423
Fine, let's expose everything, then.

470
00:37:18,517 --> 00:37:21,872
Let's expose every con you and I pulled
and let the courts decide.

471
00:37:21,897 --> 00:37:23,480
Sure, expose it all.

472
00:37:23,974 --> 00:37:25,514
You and Chairman Jang have a lot to lose.

473
00:37:25,516 --> 00:37:26,924
We've got nothing left to lose.

474
00:37:27,224 --> 00:37:29,309
Four convictions or five,
what's the difference?

475
00:37:29,417 --> 00:37:30,797
If you want to expose it, go ahead.

476
00:37:37,918 --> 00:37:39,490
Hello.

477
00:37:42,523 --> 00:37:45,430
I'm here about the part-time job.

478
00:37:45,697 --> 00:37:48,999
- You called earlier, right?
- Yes.

479
00:37:49,024 --> 00:37:50,024
Just a moment.

480
00:37:55,245 --> 00:37:57,351
I'm Lee Eun Ok.

481
00:37:57,944 --> 00:38:01,191
Hello. I'm Han Gyu Rim.

482
00:38:05,230 --> 00:38:09,035
I misread the address and had
a hard time finding this place.

483
00:38:09,244 --> 00:38:12,517
Could I possibly get an iced americano?

484
00:38:12,824 --> 00:38:16,382
We don't have a coffee machine here,

485
00:38:16,581 --> 00:38:18,481
so I'll run out and get you one.

486
00:38:18,626 --> 00:38:20,090
An iced americano?

487
00:38:20,758 --> 00:38:23,198
Yes. Decaf, if possible.

488
00:38:23,524 --> 00:38:25,435
Sure. Have a seat and relax.

489
00:38:32,830 --> 00:38:35,706
Gyu Min, Gyu Seo. Mom's here.

490
00:38:36,497 --> 00:38:38,762
Your sisters and brother
didn't pick on you, did they?

491
00:38:42,896 --> 00:38:46,109
How can Gyu Rim not notice?

492
00:38:53,119 --> 00:38:57,610
Right. She and I are
completely different people.

493
00:38:58,784 --> 00:39:00,870
No wonder even Gyu Rim can't recognize me.

494
00:39:04,021 --> 00:39:08,382
Korean plastic surgery really is
the best in the world.

495
00:39:18,044 --> 00:39:22,039
He goes to an art academy here,
and he should be coming down soon.

496
00:39:32,984 --> 00:39:35,974
Bye. See you tomorrow, Lee Da Som.

497
00:39:37,584 --> 00:39:39,362
That boy is Han Gyeol.

498
00:39:46,837 --> 00:39:48,617
What do you think, Secretary Ahn?

499
00:39:49,603 --> 00:39:51,207
Does he look like Mu Jin?

500
00:39:51,850 --> 00:39:56,346
If you're asking for my personal opinion,
yes, he does.

501
00:39:58,937 --> 00:40:00,052
Kiddo?

502
00:40:01,259 --> 00:40:02,459
Kiddo.

503
00:40:06,360 --> 00:40:07,524
Me?

504
00:40:12,597 --> 00:40:14,092
Yes, you.

505
00:40:14,356 --> 00:40:18,364
I hear a place around here makes great
spicy rice cakes. Do you know where it is?

506
00:40:18,389 --> 00:40:20,923
Spicy Rice Cake Hall of Fame?

507
00:40:21,836 --> 00:40:25,631
You mean the one that was on TV?

508
00:40:26,283 --> 00:40:27,950
Yes, that one.

509
00:40:28,693 --> 00:40:30,667
Go straight that way,

510
00:40:30,669 --> 00:40:33,684
and when you see the dry cleaner's,
just turn there.

511
00:40:35,747 --> 00:40:40,433
But honestly, that place isn't that good.

512
00:40:42,760 --> 00:40:43,911
Why?

513
00:40:44,070 --> 00:40:47,377
It was on TV, but the food's not good.

514
00:40:48,157 --> 00:40:51,185
It's just spicy,
the line's long for no reason,

515
00:40:51,541 --> 00:40:53,204
and the owner's not nice either.

516
00:40:53,734 --> 00:40:55,244
Really?

517
00:40:55,475 --> 00:40:59,923
By the way, are you team wheat cake
or team rice cake?

518
00:41:00,610 --> 00:41:03,972
Me? Rice cake.

519
00:41:04,228 --> 00:41:08,124
Then if you like rice cakes,
there's a place I'd recommend.

520
00:41:08,957 --> 00:41:11,793
My youngest aunt loves spicy rice cakes,

521
00:41:11,988 --> 00:41:13,477
and that's her favorite place.

522
00:41:13,509 --> 00:41:16,514
It's called Super Tasty,
and it's super tasty.

523
00:41:17,493 --> 00:41:21,517
If you mention Han Gyu Min,
they'll throw in a free egg.

524
00:41:22,449 --> 00:41:26,243
I see. Then I'd better go there.

525
00:41:27,528 --> 00:41:31,610
Who did you get your brains from?

526
00:41:31,714 --> 00:41:33,040
My mom.

527
00:41:35,463 --> 00:41:36,847
Not your dad?

528
00:41:37,316 --> 00:41:41,059
I don't know about my dad.

529
00:41:41,584 --> 00:41:44,358
I've never seen him.

530
00:41:46,547 --> 00:41:47,970
I see.

531
00:41:50,585 --> 00:41:51,843
Han Gyeol!

532
00:41:54,039 --> 00:41:55,384
Mom!

533
00:42:00,097 --> 00:42:01,377
Who was that?

534
00:42:02,724 --> 00:42:06,684
Some lady I don't know asked me
where to get good spicy rice cakes.

535
00:42:07,184 --> 00:42:09,068
Did you tell her nicely?

536
00:42:09,523 --> 00:42:12,751
- Of course.
- Good job.

537
00:42:13,260 --> 00:42:14,746
What did you draw at the academy today?

538
00:42:14,843 --> 00:42:16,610
- Happiness.
- Happiness?

539
00:42:16,837 --> 00:42:19,917
The teacher told us to draw happiness.

540
00:42:19,942 --> 00:42:20,942
Really?

541
00:42:21,224 --> 00:42:24,805
- So how did you draw it, Gyeol?
- I drew myself.

542
00:42:24,898 --> 00:42:27,044
You? Han Gyeol?

543
00:42:27,073 --> 00:42:29,786
Yeah. I'm happiness, Mom.

544
00:42:29,903 --> 00:42:33,396
You said so. You said I made you happy.

545
00:42:35,108 --> 00:42:38,245
That's right. Gyeol is happiness.

546
00:42:38,283 --> 00:42:40,203
So you drew happiness as yourself?

547
00:42:40,550 --> 00:42:42,892
My baby's a real genius.

548
00:42:45,778 --> 00:42:47,443
Happiness is here.

549
00:42:47,514 --> 00:42:49,392
It came right to me.

550
00:42:49,417 --> 00:42:55,154
Han Gyu Rim.
You sure raised that boy well.

551
00:42:55,610 --> 00:42:59,437
Happiness came right to me.

552
00:43:00,932 --> 00:43:03,872
Who? My Gyeol?

553
00:43:04,997 --> 00:43:06,264
Why would Gyeol be a burden...

554
00:43:06,864 --> 00:43:08,117
Actually, he is.

555
00:43:08,217 --> 00:43:10,234
Yeah, you're right. He's a burden.

556
00:43:12,077 --> 00:43:16,161
I come home smiling to myself
after seeing my son-in-law Kim,

557
00:43:16,187 --> 00:43:20,775
but whenever I think of Gyeol,
I get this tight feeling in my chest.

558
00:43:22,055 --> 00:43:23,734
Hey, let's hang up.

559
00:43:24,347 --> 00:43:28,147
The grim reaper of my house
is glaring at me.

560
00:43:28,762 --> 00:43:31,433
No, not Gyu Yeong. Someone else.

561
00:43:31,703 --> 00:43:35,682
He must've gone and recharged somewhere.
He's even fiercer than Gyu Yeong.

562
00:43:36,816 --> 00:43:40,352
Okay, call me again.

563
00:43:42,105 --> 00:43:43,709
Why is Gyeol a burden?

564
00:43:45,305 --> 00:43:48,177
Of course he is.
Is he some kind of treasure?

565
00:43:48,412 --> 00:43:50,004
Gyeol is a treasure.

566
00:43:50,059 --> 00:43:51,636
He's a treasure to Gyu Rim,

567
00:43:51,677 --> 00:43:53,444
to Gyu Min and me,

568
00:43:53,684 --> 00:43:55,523
and to Gyu O too.

569
00:43:55,525 --> 00:43:58,427
Yeah, he might be a treasure to you guys,

570
00:43:58,468 --> 00:44:00,850
but to me, he's a burden. So what?

571
00:44:01,302 --> 00:44:05,132
He's going to be the biggest obstacle
to my daughter getting married.

572
00:44:05,379 --> 00:44:07,210
- So what?
- Dad.

573
00:44:07,275 --> 00:44:10,115
Hey, my neck hurts from looking up. Sit.

574
00:44:12,169 --> 00:44:13,837
I said sit.

575
00:44:16,314 --> 00:44:17,584
Hey.

576
00:44:21,464 --> 00:44:23,717
Since we're on the subject,

577
00:44:23,992 --> 00:44:26,365
honestly, my son-in-law Kim
has never been married,

578
00:44:26,644 --> 00:44:31,715
owns that big restaurant, and has savings.
He's a five-star catch.

579
00:44:31,851 --> 00:44:34,712
Your sister is a poor woman
with nothing to show for herself,

580
00:44:34,873 --> 00:44:37,410
with a string of siblings in tow.

581
00:44:37,576 --> 00:44:40,516
Fine. Let's say that's all okay.

582
00:44:40,616 --> 00:44:44,140
Cinderella was poor and lived in an attic,

583
00:44:44,165 --> 00:44:45,757
but she married a prince.

584
00:44:46,297 --> 00:44:48,677
Sim Cheong had a blind father,

585
00:44:49,451 --> 00:44:52,417
and was too poor to offer
even a single grain of rice,

586
00:44:52,805 --> 00:44:55,862
but she married a king and became queen.

587
00:44:56,463 --> 00:44:57,463
Right?

588
00:44:58,051 --> 00:45:03,489
But do you know what Cinderella
and Sim Cheong have in common?

589
00:45:04,890 --> 00:45:10,516
What all those poor heroines
in fairy tales have in common is...

590
00:45:10,894 --> 00:45:14,529
none of them had a burden
like your sister does.

591
00:45:16,437 --> 00:45:20,717
Hey, what in-laws would be happy
about a single mom with a kid?

592
00:45:21,511 --> 00:45:24,864
If your son brought home a woman like that
as his bride someday,

593
00:45:24,919 --> 00:45:27,418
would you say,
"She's lovely. I'm thrilled,"

594
00:45:27,420 --> 00:45:29,191
and welcome her with open arms?

595
00:45:30,324 --> 00:45:33,162
But Mu Jin adores Gyeol.

596
00:45:33,997 --> 00:45:35,677
He loves him like his own son.

597
00:45:36,316 --> 00:45:37,649
Isn't that enough?

598
00:45:38,385 --> 00:45:41,565
Hey. You think it's enough
that the two of them are happy?

599
00:45:44,825 --> 00:45:48,680
When I think of my Gyu Rim
being judged because of Gyeol...

600
00:45:49,115 --> 00:45:51,126
and getting picked on
by her mother-in-law,

601
00:45:52,419 --> 00:45:54,283
I can't sleep these days. I really can't.

602
00:45:54,584 --> 00:45:56,238
Don't lie.

603
00:45:56,488 --> 00:45:58,607
You sleep just fine, snoring away.

604
00:45:59,188 --> 00:46:02,739
If Gyu Rim's in-laws don't want Gyeol,
I'll raise him myself.

605
00:46:02,917 --> 00:46:04,342
How would you raise him?

606
00:46:04,344 --> 00:46:06,108
- Aren't you going to get married?
- No, I'm not.

607
00:46:06,908 --> 00:46:07,908
Happy?

608
00:46:12,570 --> 00:46:15,097
So I'm hired, then?

609
00:46:15,636 --> 00:46:20,370
Yes. You can start
the day before the store reopens.

610
00:46:21,273 --> 00:46:24,664
Thank you.
I look forward to working with you.

611
00:46:24,737 --> 00:46:27,780
Same here.

612
00:46:29,444 --> 00:46:30,771
I'll be going, then.

613
00:46:31,177 --> 00:46:32,820
See you the day before we open.

614
00:46:32,941 --> 00:46:34,835
- Okay. Get home safe.
- Okay.

615
00:46:34,837 --> 00:46:36,610
- I'll just leave this here.
- Okay.

616
00:46:48,063 --> 00:46:49,418
Hello, son.

617
00:46:51,690 --> 00:46:53,490
Am I a burden to you, Mom?

618
00:46:54,134 --> 00:46:55,664
What do you mean?

619
00:46:55,917 --> 00:46:57,923
Who said that to you, Gyeol?

620
00:46:59,434 --> 00:47:04,316
Am I in the way of you getting married?

621
00:47:06,471 --> 00:47:08,731
It's not like that, Gyeol.

622
00:47:09,930 --> 00:47:13,299
I told you what you mean to me.

623
00:47:13,763 --> 00:47:15,553
Did you forget what I said?

624
00:47:16,330 --> 00:47:17,983
No, I didn't.

625
00:47:18,945 --> 00:47:22,982
You said when everything was dark for you,
I came and turned on the light.

626
00:47:24,016 --> 00:47:26,580
That I saved your life.

627
00:47:27,524 --> 00:47:29,471
I didn't forget a thing.

628
00:47:31,876 --> 00:47:35,904
From now on, don't listen to anyone.
Just listen to me.

629
00:47:36,517 --> 00:47:39,612
If I say it's fine,
who cares what anyone else says?

630
00:47:40,586 --> 00:47:45,857
Don't break up with Mu Jin
because of me, Mom.

631
00:47:47,704 --> 00:47:50,269
Don't do it because of me, Mom.

632
00:47:51,130 --> 00:47:53,241
Please don't, Mom.

633
00:47:54,551 --> 00:47:57,290
Okay. I won't break up with him.

634
00:47:57,543 --> 00:47:59,677
I'll never break up with him.

635
00:48:07,297 --> 00:48:09,230
I'm sorry I was such a coward.

636
00:48:10,537 --> 00:48:14,449
I'm sorry I kept running away.

637
00:48:15,658 --> 00:48:17,551
It won't happen again.

638
00:48:18,398 --> 00:48:23,149
I promise I'll never do it again,
so don't cry, baby.

639
00:48:27,895 --> 00:48:30,934
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

640
00:48:36,440 --> 00:48:37,850
Welcome.

641
00:48:42,497 --> 00:48:43,970
What is it this time?

642
00:48:50,868 --> 00:48:55,324
Why does Seong Uk keep calling me
and asking where you are?

643
00:49:03,429 --> 00:49:06,480
- Why didn't you try harder to stop me?
- Stop what?

644
00:49:07,511 --> 00:49:11,643
When I said I was marrying Kang Seong Uk,
why didn't you try harder to stop me?

645
00:49:14,477 --> 00:49:16,250
I tried plenty.

646
00:49:16,284 --> 00:49:17,997
You should've tried harder.

647
00:49:18,357 --> 00:49:20,731
You should've fought harder and longer.

648
00:49:21,305 --> 00:49:26,049
I fought hard and long,
and even paid damages for hitting him.

649
00:49:26,050 --> 00:49:28,117
You still should've tried harder.

650
00:49:28,197 --> 00:49:31,150
Even if you had to pull my hair out
or break my legs,

651
00:49:31,358 --> 00:49:32,831
you should've stopped me no matter what.

652
00:49:32,856 --> 00:49:37,384
Yes, my mistake. I'm sorry.

653
00:49:37,804 --> 00:49:39,357
Guilty as charged.

654
00:49:42,335 --> 00:49:43,936
It's Mr. Han Seok Jung's fault.

655
00:49:44,063 --> 00:49:46,317
And Han Gyu Rim's fault, and Han Gyu O's.

656
00:49:46,757 --> 00:49:51,296
Why didn't my so-called family
try harder to stop me?

657
00:49:51,909 --> 00:49:54,018
They should've stopped me,
even if they had to hit me.

658
00:49:54,177 --> 00:49:56,524
Even if they had to lock me in my room.

659
00:49:57,984 --> 00:49:59,904
My life went down the drain like this...

660
00:49:59,978 --> 00:50:03,797
because of you, and Mr. Han Seok Jung,
and Han Gyu Rim, and Han Gyu O.

661
00:50:06,951 --> 00:50:09,237
Does blaming others make you feel better?

662
00:50:12,804 --> 00:50:14,444
What did I do wrong?

663
00:50:15,198 --> 00:50:16,544
Liking money?

664
00:50:17,191 --> 00:50:19,131
Wanting to move up in the world?

665
00:50:19,410 --> 00:50:21,863
Go ask anyone walking by.

666
00:50:22,029 --> 00:50:25,674
Ask if there's anyone who hates money
and doesn't want to climb higher.

667
00:50:25,863 --> 00:50:27,744
Go ask every one of them.

668
00:50:28,071 --> 00:50:31,790
Nothing wrong with the goal.
It's how you go about it.

669
00:50:32,110 --> 00:50:35,942
Just because someone likes money
and wants to get ahead,

670
00:50:36,102 --> 00:50:37,941
it doesn't mean they live like you.

671
00:50:40,618 --> 00:50:44,884
Have you ever been broke?

672
00:50:46,530 --> 00:50:49,381
Ever gone from rich princess
to beggar overnight,

673
00:50:50,422 --> 00:50:55,512
and been rejected, ignored, and cut off
by the person you liked?

674
00:50:57,176 --> 00:50:59,389
Ever been handed money for tuition
and school lunches,

675
00:50:59,630 --> 00:51:02,376
like spare change tossed to a beggar?

676
00:51:04,217 --> 00:51:06,451
I didn't have money,

677
00:51:07,019 --> 00:51:09,089
so when my dad fell off a cliff,

678
00:51:09,144 --> 00:51:11,740
he died without getting proper surgery,

679
00:51:13,455 --> 00:51:15,632
but I didn't end up living like you.

680
00:51:18,083 --> 00:51:20,723
Fine, aren't you something.

681
00:51:20,844 --> 00:51:24,144
That's why you're still living
the way you are.

682
00:51:32,436 --> 00:51:34,071
Hey, Gyu Yeong!

683
00:51:34,166 --> 00:51:37,343
What's wrong? Are you okay?

684
00:51:42,397 --> 00:51:45,190
What brings you all the way here, ma'am?

685
00:51:45,215 --> 00:51:48,075
What, am I not allowed
in places like this?

686
00:51:48,100 --> 00:51:51,093
What do you mean?

687
00:51:51,183 --> 00:51:55,715
I'm just so happy you'd come all this way.

688
00:51:55,740 --> 00:51:58,778
You're so tall, my neck's killing me.

689
00:51:59,117 --> 00:52:01,998
So tall it's rude.

690
00:52:02,036 --> 00:52:07,487
Then today, I'll give you
something on the house,

691
00:52:07,629 --> 00:52:10,080
so take your time and enjoy.

692
00:52:10,136 --> 00:52:15,734
Of course. People around here
sure are generous.

693
00:52:16,351 --> 00:52:18,151
That's right.

694
00:52:27,744 --> 00:52:30,149
I'll be going now,

695
00:52:30,174 --> 00:52:34,757
so take your time with the menu,
and call me when you're ready.

696
00:52:35,051 --> 00:52:37,221
Sure, thanks.

697
00:52:46,650 --> 00:52:49,436
Even the water's good.

698
00:52:50,560 --> 00:52:53,012
What would you like, Su Nam?
It's on me today.

699
00:52:53,097 --> 00:52:55,724
What? I already paid in advance.

700
00:52:55,749 --> 00:52:57,335
In advance?

701
00:52:57,982 --> 00:53:01,123
What looks good?

702
00:53:01,124 --> 00:53:02,957
This shrimp...

703
00:53:02,982 --> 00:53:04,451
Goodness. It's all in English.

704
00:53:04,488 --> 00:53:07,277
Dear me, what am I going to do?

705
00:53:07,291 --> 00:53:10,058
I put the pressure cooker
in the chicken soup...

706
00:53:10,118 --> 00:53:14,556
I mean, I left chicken soup cooking
in the pressure cooker and totally forgot.

707
00:53:14,591 --> 00:53:16,404
What do I do?

708
00:53:16,437 --> 00:53:19,184
You left chicken soup cooking
when you came out to eat?

709
00:53:19,209 --> 00:53:20,247
Yes.

710
00:53:20,277 --> 00:53:21,417
Isn't Heung Sik home?

711
00:53:21,419 --> 00:53:24,437
No. My house is going to catch fire.

712
00:53:24,462 --> 00:53:26,384
I need to run back quickly,
so order anything.

713
00:53:26,386 --> 00:53:29,446
No, order the best thing and start eating.

714
00:53:29,471 --> 00:53:31,306
Su Nam.

715
00:53:52,837 --> 00:53:54,523
Why isn't she back yet?

716
00:54:28,084 --> 00:54:31,557
Hello, you must be Han Gyu O?

717
00:54:33,550 --> 00:54:37,557
I'm Kwon Hui Na. Park Su Nam set us up.

718
00:54:40,751 --> 00:54:42,791
Why do you look so flustered?

719
00:54:44,100 --> 00:54:47,568
You didn't know this was a blind date?

720
00:54:52,070 --> 00:54:54,396
I fell for you the moment I saw you.

721
00:54:56,137 --> 00:55:00,003
Can I ask you on a second date
before we even start?

722
00:55:25,382 --> 00:55:26,864
Hello.

723
00:55:50,041 --> 00:55:53,978
Hello. You're Mu Jin's mother, right?

724
00:55:56,183 --> 00:55:57,277
Han Gyu Rim?

725
00:55:59,457 --> 00:56:03,063
Yes, I'm Han Gyu Rim.

726
00:56:19,923 --> 00:56:21,923
Why aren't you saying anything?

727
00:56:24,011 --> 00:56:28,451
Why did you come all this way to see me?

728
00:56:32,956 --> 00:56:36,176
Didn't you come because you had
something to say to me?

729
00:57:06,117 --> 00:57:07,926
Are you planning to sit here all night?

730
00:57:15,783 --> 00:57:18,746
I came to take back what I said.

731
00:57:21,836 --> 00:57:24,163
I can't leave Mu Jin.

732
00:57:25,141 --> 00:57:29,027
I need to be by his side.

733
00:57:30,877 --> 00:57:35,104
I tried hard to run away,
but there's nowhere left to run,

734
00:57:37,109 --> 00:57:39,331
and I don't want to run anymore.

735
00:57:40,921 --> 00:57:44,651
Look here, Han Gyu Rim.

736
00:57:47,104 --> 00:57:51,893
When I try to stop Mu Jin,
that just makes him care more.

737
00:57:52,281 --> 00:57:57,425
When I hide, it hurts him more.
When I run, he wants me even more.

738
00:57:59,064 --> 00:58:04,870
Whatever I do, he never gets tired of it.
That's just how Mu Jin is.

739
00:58:09,131 --> 00:58:13,149
If we see this through to the end
and it turns out it's not meant to be,

740
00:58:13,625 --> 00:58:15,933
I'll walk away without looking back.

741
00:58:17,257 --> 00:58:21,269
If we see it through
and it just won't work,

742
00:58:21,666 --> 00:58:25,737
I'll walk away without any regret,
resentment, or disappointment.

743
00:58:27,110 --> 00:58:30,236
Only when we see it through
will Mu Jin accept it,

744
00:58:30,331 --> 00:58:32,331
and only then will he let me go.

745
00:58:40,442 --> 00:58:41,723
And...

746
00:58:45,963 --> 00:58:50,453
I also need to see it through,

747
00:58:51,054 --> 00:58:55,716
see it through for real,
so I can end things with Mu Jin.

748
00:58:57,157 --> 00:58:58,710
I'm sorry.

749
00:58:59,699 --> 00:59:02,158
Please take back what you said
about cutting ties with him,

750
00:59:02,886 --> 00:59:05,198
and give us your permission
to be together.

751
00:59:07,117 --> 00:59:10,606
Please help us so that if it has to end,

752
00:59:13,236 --> 00:59:14,709
we can be the ones to end it.

753
01:00:17,223 --> 01:00:19,457
(Sister)

754
01:00:25,713 --> 01:00:27,037
Hello?

755
01:00:27,631 --> 01:00:30,393
Han Gyu Rim came to my house?
To see our mom.

756
01:00:30,782 --> 01:00:32,337
Did you send her?

757
01:00:32,730 --> 01:00:34,023
Gyu Rim did?

758
01:00:35,189 --> 01:00:37,740
She's gotten really gutsy.

759
01:00:38,083 --> 01:00:39,953
She's not the Han Gyu Rim I used to know.

760
01:01:01,364 --> 01:01:03,679
- Hey, Mu Jin.
- Where are you?

761
01:01:04,117 --> 01:01:05,579
Where are you right now?

762
01:01:21,964 --> 01:01:23,917
What's wrong, Ok Seon?

763
01:01:24,517 --> 01:01:26,117
Drinking alone at this hour?

764
01:01:26,917 --> 01:01:28,900
I'm just in a lousy mood.

765
01:01:29,130 --> 01:01:31,723
Why? Did someone say something to you?

766
01:01:33,381 --> 01:01:35,576
Who was it?
I'll go give them a piece of my mind.

767
01:01:39,517 --> 01:01:42,420
I want to smack that mouth of hers,

768
01:01:42,445 --> 01:01:44,691
but what's the point?

769
01:01:45,385 --> 01:01:48,992
I want to slap her across the face,
but what's the point?

770
01:01:50,254 --> 01:01:54,177
I want to give her a good pinch,
but what's the point?

771
01:01:55,277 --> 01:01:58,283
That sounds like depression
mixed with helplessness.

772
01:01:59,830 --> 01:02:03,406
I'm depressed. I'm very depressed.

773
01:02:04,197 --> 01:02:05,770
Depressed? That'll be 50 cents.

774
01:02:10,864 --> 01:02:12,943
Put 50 cents in here.

775
01:02:13,764 --> 01:02:16,675
- I don't have cash. Do you take cards?
- Yes.

776
01:02:30,331 --> 01:02:33,011
- Pay in full.
- Okay.

777
01:02:43,170 --> 01:02:46,626
<i>Love is leaving</i>

778
01:02:46,701 --> 01:02:50,109
<i>Leaving my side once again</i>

779
01:02:50,278 --> 01:02:53,280
<i>This time I began</i>

780
01:02:53,305 --> 01:02:57,134
<i>It was finally love</i>

781
01:02:57,357 --> 01:03:00,597
<i>Too much</i>

782
01:03:00,684 --> 01:03:04,524
<i>Is not what I want</i>

783
01:03:04,631 --> 01:03:10,884
<i>Did I want too much</i>

784
01:03:11,450 --> 01:03:13,343
That's 50 cents' worth.

785
01:03:19,096 --> 01:03:21,176
What on earth are you?

786
01:03:22,583 --> 01:03:24,663
Someone you can't get over.

787
01:03:25,157 --> 01:03:27,990
Once you fall for me, there's no way out.

788
01:03:34,990 --> 01:03:36,266
Gyu Rim.

789
01:03:43,284 --> 01:03:44,464
Are you okay?

790
01:03:47,277 --> 01:03:48,510
I'm okay.

791
01:03:50,010 --> 01:03:51,593
Why did you go see my mother?

792
01:03:53,736 --> 01:03:57,018
I kept hiding behind you and running away.

793
01:03:57,983 --> 01:04:00,603
I felt like such a coward.

794
01:04:02,090 --> 01:04:03,690
What did you talk about?

795
01:04:05,177 --> 01:04:07,806
I told her I'd go all the way with you...

796
01:04:08,287 --> 01:04:12,506
and see how we end up.

797
01:04:15,563 --> 01:04:17,934
Promise me one thing, Mu Jin.

798
01:04:20,057 --> 01:04:22,840
Let's see this through and burn it all,

799
01:04:23,620 --> 01:04:26,410
burn it all until there aren't
even ashes left,

800
01:04:29,404 --> 01:04:32,804
and if it's still not right,
then let's stop.

801
01:04:32,943 --> 01:04:37,200
Without blaming anyone
or holding any grudges.

802
01:05:40,760 --> 01:05:43,406
(Love on the Menu)

803
01:05:43,431 --> 01:05:45,237
Why are you keeping quiet?

804
01:05:45,262 --> 01:05:46,953
You're curious about so much,

805
01:05:47,018 --> 01:05:49,497
so why have you never asked what I do?

806
01:05:49,522 --> 01:05:51,337
- Hide me, please.
- What are you talking about?

807
01:05:51,362 --> 01:05:52,497
If they catch me, I'm dead.

808
01:05:52,522 --> 01:05:53,610
- I'll protect you.
- I'm saved.

809
01:05:53,635 --> 01:05:55,573
If my daughter is your daughter-in-law,
then what does that make us?

810
01:05:55,666 --> 01:05:59,046
It's my life to live.
Can't you just trust me?

811
01:05:59,071 --> 01:06:01,084
Is Han Gyu Rim really that great?

812
01:06:01,109 --> 01:06:03,262
You know you can't break his stubbornness.

813
01:06:03,287 --> 01:06:05,030
He'll die at this rate.

814
01:06:05,055 --> 01:06:07,070
I love you too, Mu Jin.

815
01:06:07,703 --> 01:06:09,503
Dramaday.me
